.0001305426994804293, "top": [["_COMPILER", -0.0001305426994804293], ["/compiler", -10.499687194824219]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.00028357948758639395, "top": [["=", -0.00028357948758639395], [" ic", -11.615891456604004]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -0.0003319337556604296, "top": [["ic", -0.0003319337556604296], [" ic", -8.568279266357422]]}, {"t": "x", "lp": -0.0018575744470581412, "top": [["x", -0.0018575744470581412], [" -", -8.186145782470703]]}, {"t": " -", "lp": -0.005719596054404974, "top": [[" -", -0.005719596054404974], ["\n", -5.237772464752197]]}, {"t": "DC", "lp": -8.273466664832085e-05, "top": [["DC", -8.273466664832085e-05], [" DC", -10.145297050476074]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables. The `--force` flag re-initializes the environment even if it was already set. This is essential because the compiler (`icx`/`icpx`) and SYCL runtime need proper PATH, library, and environment configuration to function.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the shell exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status. A build failure stops the build rather than continuing with broken state.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\nThe `cmake` command configures the build. Let me flag each argument:\n\n### Generator & Paths\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`** \u2014 Source directory (the cloned repo)\n- **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`** \u2014 Build output directory (kept inside srcdir, not the standard build/ dir)\n- **`-G Ninja`** \u2014 Use the Ninja generator (fast, specified in `makedepends`)\n\n### Build Type & Installation\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimized build with `-O3`-style optimizations (no debug symbols).\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\nInstall binaries to `/usr` and libraries to `/usr/lib` (note the `lib`, not `lib64`).\n\n### The Compilers\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DC"}